Description: HTTP/3 over Rustls, through ngtcp2 and the rustls-ffi-quic library
 Lets --with-rustls --with-ngtcp2 --with-nghttp3 build, with a TLS backend that
 is not OpenSSL, GnuTLS or wolfSSL:
 - lib/vtls/rustls.c: the client config is built by cr_build_config(), which
   takes the ALPN list and the origin instead of reading them from the TLS
   connection filter, so that the QUIC filter can build it too;
   Curl_rustls_quic_ctx_init() and _free() are the QUIC side of it.
 - lib/vquic/: the Rustls branch of vquic-tls.[ch] and cf-ngtcp2*.[ch]. The
   TLS session is the one of ngtcp2_crypto_rustls (libngtcp2_crypto_rustls).
 - configure: the pkg-config module rustls-quic (rustls-ffi-quic, whose
   functions are named rustlsq_*) is used when it is there and rustls-ffi
   otherwise; with rustls-quic, QUIC is on, and the ngtcp2 crypto helper
   libngtcp2_crypto_rustls is looked up like the ones for the other backends.
 Against plain rustls-ffi nothing changes: no QUIC, the same functions called.
Author: Marie <289302950+marie-222@users.noreply.github.com>
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-30
